// error
// #6479: a strict cell is `@threadlocal` (or in a runtime/ module); a plain module
// cell outside runtime/ now takes any type and any initializer.
// The other half of #1430: an initializer that genuinely is not constant must
// be refused by `bit check`, and the diagnostic must point at the DECLARATION.
//
// Previously the self-hosted compiler accepted this at check time and failed
// during lowering with "cannot lower 1 function(s): main" — naming a function
// that is entirely correct, while the faulty `let` went unmentioned. The span
// here is the initializer, so the error lands on the line that has to change.
@threadlocal let x: i64 = compute()

fn compute(): i64 {
  return 1
}

fn main() {
  print("${x}\n")
}
